Z||000000||ponya||10-19-2000||07:40 PM||||Getting ready to change dew strips. I was just thumbing thru my P-22 parts book when I saw that there is window stabilizer that works on the opposite side of the dew strips. It also shows a pad that the window slides against and stabilizes the window. Went to Pontiac today and that part is unavailable. Does anyone know what I could use to re-face the stabilizer pad. Would heavy felt work? Need something that wont scratch the window. Any idea's appreciated.  Thanks   Bob||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||10-19-2000||07:52 PM||||Depends....if you're refering to the two (or is it three, I forget) small ones that screw in, then I suppose you could use felt pieces that are adhesive on one side. If you're referring to the long piece on the inside (the inner dew wipe I guess), then you could prob go to a fabric store and buy some long strips of felt to cover it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||10-19-2000||11:15 PM||||Those pads are glued on a small bracket that is held on by one stud/nut.  I'd look to find another one from a junk door in the boneyard.  Not sure if that braket is common with other GM cars, it could be.  You might be able to find one from a Chevette or S-10 that's identical or has similar dimensions.  It just might work because those are have an adjustable slot in the door.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">           <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
